# Normalise every text file to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this the repository was a mix: most sources LF, a few files CRLF, and no rule saying which.
# Nothing in the build cares, so a tool that rewrote a file with the other ending went unnoticed until
# git reported every line of it as changed -- Python's text mode on Windows does exactly that, and it
# once turned a fifty-line edit into a five-thousand-line diff. Pinning eol=lf makes that impossible
# rather than merely discouraged: a rewritten file comes back to LF on checkout either way.
#
# .NET, MSBuild, Avalonia and Visual Studio all read LF happily on Windows, so nothing here needs CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries, so git never inspects or converts their contents.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
